From: meta-ossia
Subject: [PATCH] vst3: define PlugFrame on Linux without xcb

vst3::PlugFrame has three implementations, selected by preprocessor guards:
one for _WIN32, one for __APPLE__, and the X11 one in Linux/PlugFrame.hpp
behind __has_include(<xcb/xcb.h>). On a Linux target built without X11 -- no
xcb headers in the sysroot -- none of the three is selected, the forward
declaration in WindowContainer.hpp is all that remains, and Window.cpp fails
with "allocation of incomplete type 'PlugFrame'".

Widen the first guard so the no-op implementation also covers Linux without
xcb. It is the same shape as the _WIN32 one: the plugin's own window is not
embedded, which is what a headless image wants anyway.

Fixed differently upstream, by merging the two blocks into a single guard
`defined(_WIN32) || defined(__APPLE__) || !__has_include(<xcb/xcb.h>)`. This
keeps the change minimal against the 3.8.2 release so it applies cleanly.

Upstream-Status: Backport

--- a/src/plugins/score-plugin-vst3/Vst3/UI/PlugFrame.hpp
+++ b/src/plugins/score-plugin-vst3/Vst3/UI/PlugFrame.hpp
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 namespace vst3
 {
 
-#if defined(_WIN32)
+#if defined(_WIN32) || (!defined(__APPLE__) && !__has_include(<xcb/xcb.h>))
 class PlugFrame final : public Steinberg::IPlugFrame
 {
 public:
